Subject: [PATCH] Wire real HRPT permit data into the field-detail page
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The page was showing a static "Spordo does not have access to their
live availability data" card for every HRPT field, even though the
data has existed in D1 since the earlier port. The actual display
logic (loadPermitInfoCard, fetchPermitMeta/fetchCachedPermits) already
existed but was dead code: never called, and pointed at Supabase
tables that were never populated for HRPT.

- Add GET /api/permits/:fieldId (src/permitsApi.js), reading D1
  server-side (browsers can't reach D1 directly the way they could
  Supabase's public REST API).
- Repoint the frontend fetchers at that route instead of Supabase.
- Fix loadPermitInfoCard's availability check, which unconditionally
  treated every HRPT/external field as "unavailable" regardless of
  whether real synced data existed for it — a leftover assumption
  from before the scraper was built.
- Actually call loadPermitInfoCard from renderSchdBody's external-field
  branch, and fix a copy bug (f.org, never set anywhere) that showed
  a blank space in the card.
- Fix package.json's test glob: node --test src/**/*.test.js was
  unquoted, so bash (globstar off) expanded ** as a single directory
  level, silently skipping any test file placed directly in src/ (as
  opposed to src/hrpt/*). Quoting it lets Node's own glob handle **
  correctly.
